  q(CHAIR,'Decay on the proximal surface of an anterior tooth that does not involve the incisal angle is which G.V. Black class?','Class III',['Class I','Class IV, which includes the incisal angle','Class II'],'B','Class III lesions are on proximal surfaces of incisors and canines and are often restored with composite.',BOYD),
  q(CHAIR,'Decay on the cervical third of the facial surface of a tooth is which class?','Class V',['Class II','Class III','Class VI, which involves the incisal edges or cusp tips'],'C','Class V lesions sit near the gumline on facial or lingual surfaces and may come from decay or abrasion.',BOYD),
  q(CHAIR,'Which bur shape is often used to remove decay and to open into the tooth?','Round bur',['Inverted cone bur','Straight fissure bur','A finishing bur used only to smooth composite after curing'],'D','Round burs come in many sizes and are used for removing decay and starting the preparation.',BOYD),
  q(CHAIR,'Which bur is pear-shaped and commonly used in amalgam and composite preparations?','#330 bur',['#557 bur','#1/2 bur','A diamond wheel used to section a crown off a tooth'],'A','The #330 pear-shaped bur has a rounded end that helps create smooth internal walls in the preparation.',BOYD),
  q(CHAIR,'Which simple isolation method helps keep a tooth dry by absorbing saliva?','Cotton rolls',['Articulating paper','A matrix band','A wedge placed between teeth to seal the gingival margin'],'B','Cotton rolls are placed near the salivary duct openings to absorb moisture during short procedures.',BOYD),
  q(CHAIR,'Which hand cutting instrument bevels the gingival margin of a Class II preparation?','Gingival margin trimmer',['Spoon excavator','Burnisher','Explorer'],'C','Gingival margin trimmers have curved blades made in pairs for the mesial and distal walls.',BOYD),
  q(CHAIR,'How should scrap amalgam be stored in the dental office?','In a tightly sealed, labeled container',['In the regular trash','Poured down the sink drain','In an open cup on the counter until it is collected'],'D','Amalgam contains mercury, so scrap is sealed in a labeled container and sent for recycling.',ROB),
  q(CHAIR,'In composite bonding, what is applied after the tooth is etched and rinsed?','A primer and adhesive (bonding agent)',['Zinc oxide eugenol','Alginate','Petroleum jelly to keep the tooth moist'],'A','The bonding agent flows into the etched enamel; eugenol is avoided because it blocks resin from setting.',ROB),
  q(CHAIR,'Which material is commonly used to make a provisional crown chairside?','Bis-acryl composite',['Gypsum stone','Alginate','Gutta-percha, which is used to fill the root canal'],'B','Bis-acryl provisionals protect the prepared tooth and hold its space until the final crown is ready.',ROB),
  q(CHAIR,'Which tray is made to fit one patient’s mouth for a more accurate final impression?','A custom tray',['A stock plastic tray','A bite block','A rubber dam frame used to hold the dam away from the face'],'C','Custom trays leave an even space for impression material, which improves accuracy for crowns and dentures.',ROB),
  q(CHAIR,'Which fluoride product is painted on the teeth and sets when it contacts saliva?','Fluoride varnish',['Fluoride mouth rinse','Prescription fluoride toothpaste used at home','Fluoride gel in a foam tray'],'D','Fluoride varnish is quick to apply, sticks to the teeth and is often used for young children.',ROB),
  q(CHAIR,'How do extraction forceps differ from elevators?','Forceps grasp and remove the tooth, while elevators loosen it',['Forceps cut bone','Forceps are used only for implants','Elevators hold sutures and clamp tissue during surgery'],'A','Elevators loosen the tooth from its ligament, and forceps with shaped beaks then remove it.',BOYD),
  q(CHAIR,'What is the purpose of a rubber stop on an endodontic file?','To mark the working length of the canal',['To make the file bend','To clean the file','To protect the dentist’s finger from the sharp tip of the file'],'B','The stop marks the measured length so the file does not go past the root apex.',BOYD),
  q(CHAIR,'What is a periodontal dressing used for after gum surgery?','To protect the surgical site while it heals',['To whiten the teeth','To take an impression','To fill a cavity on the biting surface of a molar'],'C','A periodontal dressing acts like a bandage over the surgical site and is usually removed after about a week.',ROB),
  q(CHAIR,'In a dental implant, which part connects the implant body to the crown?','The abutment',['The pontic','The matrix','The clasp that grips a tooth on a removable partial denture'],'D','The implant body sits in the bone, the abutment attaches to it, and the crown is placed on the abutment.',ROB),
  q(RAD,'What does a dosimeter badge worn by dental staff measure?','The amount of radiation the worker has been exposed to',['The patient’s total X-ray dose','The temperature of the darkroom','The voltage of the X-ray machine during each exposure'],'A','Dosimeter badges are worn at work and checked regularly to make sure staff stay below the dose limit.',ROB),
  q(RAD,'A film image shows a herringbone pattern and looks light. What happened?','The film was placed backward in the mouth',['The film was exposed twice','The film was never exposed','The patient moved during the exposure, making it blurry'],'B','When the film is reversed, the pattern of the lead foil backing shows through on the image.',ROB),
  q(RAD,'In the paralleling technique, how are the receptor and tooth positioned?','Parallel to each other, with the beam at a right angle to both',['At a 90-degree angle to each other','The receptor is placed outside the mouth','Angled so the beam aims at the bisector between them'],'C','Paralleling gives the most accurate image with the least distortion of tooth size and shape.',ROB),
  q(RAD,'How is a digital sensor protected from cross-contamination between patients?','It is covered with a new disposable barrier sleeve',['It is put in the autoclave','It is soaked in water','It is wiped with a dry towel and reused without a cover'],'D','Most sensors cannot be heat sterilized, so they are covered with barriers and disinfected after use.',ROB),
  q(RAD,'Which imaging gives a three-dimensional view of the jaws for implant planning?','Cone beam computed tomography (CBCT)',['A bitewing','A periapical film','An occlusal film that shows the floor of the mouth'],'A','CBCT shows bone width, bone height and nerve location in three dimensions before implant surgery.',ROB),
  q(EMER,'A patient with diabetes has fruity breath, deep breathing and confusion. Which condition is likely?','Hyperglycemia that may lead to ketoacidosis',['Hypoglycemia from skipping a meal','Syncope from anxiety','An allergic reaction to latex gloves'],'B','Fruity breath and deep breathing point to high blood sugar, and the patient needs emergency medical care.',ROB),
  q(EMER,'A patient has crushing chest pain that nitroglycerin does not relieve. What should the team do?','Call 911, give oxygen and have the patient chew aspirin if not allergic',['Continue the procedure','Give the patient a sugary drink','Lay the patient flat and wait 30 minutes'],'C','Chest pain not relieved by nitroglycerin may be a heart attack, so EMS is called right away.',ROB),
  q(EMER,'A patient feels dizzy when the chair is raised quickly after a long procedure. What is this called?','Postural (orthostatic) hypotension',['Hyperventilation','Angina','An asthma attack with wheezing and trouble breathing'],'D','Raising the chair slowly and letting the patient sit for a moment before standing helps prevent it.',ROB),
  q(EMER,'Which device delivers high-concentration oxygen to a breathing patient in distress?','A nonrebreather mask',['A saliva ejector','A rubber dam','A nasal hood used for nitrous oxide sedation'],'A','A nonrebreather mask at a high flow rate delivers the most oxygen to a patient who is still breathing.',ROB),
  q(EMER,'A small crown slips and the patient swallows it without choking. What should happen next?','Refer the patient for an X-ray to see whether it was swallowed or inhaled',['Ignore it','Give the patient milk to drink','Tell the patient to return in 6 months'],'B','An object that enters the airway can cause serious lung problems even when the patient does not choke.',ROB)
